{"title":"Career Roadmap · Occupational Therapist","role":"Occupational Therapist","summary":"An Occupational Therapist (OT) helps people improve or regain their ability to perform everyday activities after injury, illness, disability, developmental difficulties, or functional limitations.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences — BOT (Bachelor of Occupational Therapy)","Course":"Occupational Therapy"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Occupational Therapist (OT) helps people improve or regain their ability to perform everyday activities after injury, illness, disability, developmental difficulties, or functional limitations."},{"type":"p","text":"OT interventions may focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Activities of daily living"},{"text":"Fine-motor skills"},{"text":"Gross-motor function"},{"text":"Cognitive skills"},{"text":"Sensory processing"},{"text":"Upper-limb rehabilitation"},{"text":"Neurological rehabilitation"},{"text":"Paediatric development"},{"text":"Mental-health functioning"},{"text":"Workplace and ergonomic adaptation"},{"text":"Assistive devices"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A BOT graduate can work across hospitals, rehabilitation centres, paediatric clinics, schools, community programmes, mental-health settings, elderly-care facilities, and private practice, subject to applicable professional registration and local regulations."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2028"},{"text":"Anatomy, physiology, psychology and OT fundamentals"}],[{"text":"2028–2030"},{"text":"Assessment, therapeutic activities and supervised clinical practice"}],[{"text":"2030–2032"},{"text":"Neurological, orthopaedic, paediatric and community OT"}],[{"text":"2032–2035"},{"text":"Independent clinical practice / specialist OT pathway"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Senior OT, clinical specialist or rehabilitation coordinator"}],[{"text":"2040+"},{"text":"OT clinic leadership, rehabilitation management, teaching or research"}]]}]},{"heading":"Year 1 — Biomedical & Occupational Therapy Foundation","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Build a strong foundation in human function."},{"type":"h","text":"Core subjects"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Anatomy"},{"text":"Physiology"},{"text":"Biochemistry"},{"text":"Psychology"},{"text":"Sociology"},{"text":"Pathology"},{"text":"Introduction to occupational therapy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"OT fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Occupation"},{"text":"Activity"},{"text":"Participation"},{"text":"Functional independence"},{"text":"Disability"},{"text":"Rehabilitation"},{"text":"Activity analysis"},{"text":"Patient-centred care"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Basic clinical skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient communication"},{"text":"Vital-sign awareness"},{"text":"Basic assessment"},{"text":"Positioning"},{"text":"Transfer techniques"},{"text":"Infection prevention"},{"text":"Clinical documentation"},{"text":"Professional ethics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Assessment & Therapeutic Intervention"},{"type":"p","text":"Move from theoretical knowledge to functional assessment."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn assessment of"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Range of motion"},{"text":"Muscle strength"},{"text":"Coordination"},{"text":"Balance"},{"text":"Fine motor skills"},{"text":"Gross motor skills"},{"text":"Sensory function"},{"text":"Cognitive function"},{"text":"Activities of daily living"},{"text":"Functional independence"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Activity analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to break an activity into:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Activity","Physical Requirements","Cognitive Requirements","Sensory Requirements","Environmental Requirements","Patient Limitation","Therapeutic Modification"]},{"ty